{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_bdrk_01SkLy3ZxanTD3xWxpVUk9KX","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Rust translation of c_src/src/luggage.c\n2\t// Original C by Jan Wrobel <wrr@mixedbit.org>\n3\t//\n4\t// The translation reproduces the observable behaviour of the C program\n5\t// byte-for-byte, including the quirks of the original `scanf()` usage\n6\t// (buffers that keep stale values when a conversion fails, records that are\n7\t// silently dropped when EOF is reached in the middle of a line, `%d` being\n8\t// used for an `unsigned int`, ...).\n9\t\n10\tuse std::io::{self, Read, Write};\n11\t\n12\tconst LUGGAGE_ID_LENGTH: usize = 8;\n13\tconst FLIGHT_ID_LENGTH: usize = 6;\n14\tconst AIRPORT_CODE_LENGTH: usize = 3;\n15\tconst COMMENTS_LENGTH: usize = 80;\n16\t\n17\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n18\t// C string helpers\n19\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n20\t\n21\t/// Emulates `strcpy()` from a scanf destination buffer: the C buffers are NUL\n22\t/// terminated character arrays, so copying stops at the first NUL byte.\n23\tfn c_str(bytes: &[u8]) -> Vec<u8> {\n24\t    match bytes.iter().position(|&b| b == 0) {\n25\t        Some(i) => bytes[..i].to_vec(),\n26\t        None => bytes.to_vec(),\n27\t    }\n28\t}\n29\t\n30\t/// Emulates `strcmp(a, b) == 0` for NUL terminated strings.\n31\tfn c_str_eq(a: &[u8], b: &[u8]) -> bool {\n32\t    c_str(a) == c_str(b)\n33\t}\n34\t\n35\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n36\t// scanf() emulation\n37\t// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n38\t\n39\t/// Result of a single conversion directive.\n40\tenum Conv {\n41\t    /// The conversion succeeded and a value was assigned.\n42\t    Assigned,\n43\t    /// Matching failure: nothing was assigned, the destination is untouched.\n44\t    MatchFail,\n45\t    /// Input