{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_aldp4mcldrufkbllvdywpebcs5yuffti6eln3vodo73l5zpf6syq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 66 tests pass across every configuration. Verification is complete.\n\n## What the code actually is\n\n`c_src/CMakeLists.txt` builds an **executable** (`add_executable(driver src/luggage.c)`) — a luggage-routing directive filter that parses records from stdin with `scanf` and prints the non-superseded ones matching four argv filters. `Cargo.toml` has **no `[features]`**, so there is exactly one feature combination (verified as `--no-default-features`, default, and `--all-features`, in debug and release).\n\n## Phase A artifacts (all in the crate root)\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — the C artifact is an executable, so `nm -D` on it lists only libc imports. To still test through a real `.so` boundary I built the *pristine* C translation unit as a shared library using **compiler flags only** (`gcc -shared -fPIC -O0 -Dmain=luggage_main`), and gave the Rust crate a matching `cdylib` (`src/lib.rs`) exporting the **same six symbols**. Symbol diff (C minus Rust) is **empty**.\n- **`ERRORS.md`** — 44 rows, mechanically derived (every `exit(1)`, every `== EOF` check, every non-EOF matching failure, every width limit, every `%d` range boundary, the `NULL` checks, `SIGPIPE`). No enums / `#ifdef`s / asserts exist in the C (verified with `grep -c`).\n- **`CONFIGS.md`** — 42 rows over the axes the C branches on (filters, record counts, timestamp shapes, field widths, separators, comment shapes, supersede structures, insertion positions, EOF positions, and **each low-level exported function**).\n\n## Phases B–D\n\n`tests/differential_exec.rs` (57 tests) runs both **executables** as subprocesses and compares stdout/stderr/exit status byte-for-byte; `tests/differential_ffi.rs` + `tests/differential_ffi_print.rs` (9 tests) **`libloading`-load both `.so`s** and call only their exported C symbols (~9 700 randomized calls, fixed seeds), including `printMatchingDirectives` with fd-1 capture. `./check_all.sh` automates check/build/symbol-diff/test for every combination.\n\n## Two real divergences found and fixed\n\n1. **`SIGPIPE`**: C starts with `SIG_DFL`, Rust's runtime sets `SIG_IGN`, so `driver … | head -c 20` exited **141** (C) vs **0** (Rust). Fixed in `src/main.rs`; regression-covered by `p32`.\n2. **Allocation-heavy `c_str`/`superseded`** made a 100 k-record input take >120 s vs C's ~50 s; now slice-based (output byte-identical).\n\nI also proved the suite isn't vacuous: six injected mutations (tie ordering, `%010u` width, supersede early-stop, `matches` wildcard, NUL truncation, SIGPIPE) were each caught, then reverted.\n\nOne documented deviation remains, for **undefined behaviour only**: `addRoutingDirectiveToList(NULL,…)`, `superseded(NULL)`, `matches(NULL,…)` SIGSEGV in C (verified, status 139); the Rust exports return safely. These are unreachable from the program itself; the *defined* NULL cases (`supersedes(NULL,…)` → 0, `printMatchingDirectives(NULL,…)` → no output) are asserted equal. `c_src/` is unmodified (only the instructed `c_src/build/` was added)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1870,"cache_read_input_tokens":218578,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1870,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"419e6be5-3675-4ebb-83ec-0c54728d00a3","uuid":"d61cc310-fa73-449f-81a9-f2bf20001913","timestamp":"2026-08-20T18:41:36.574Z"}
